  "question": {
    "text": "Two loudspeakers M and N are located 20m apart and emit sound at frequencies 118 Hz and 121 Hz, respectively. A car is initially at a point P, 1800 m away from the midpoint Q of the line MN and moves towards Q constantly at 60 km/hr along the perpendicular bisector of MN. It crosses Q and eventually reaches a point R, 1800 m away from Q. Let <math><mi>&#965;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> represent the beat frequency measured by a person sitting in the car at time t. Let <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#957;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>&#957;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>&#957;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></msub></math> be the beat frequencies measured at locations P, Q and R, respectively. The speed of sound in air is <math><mn>330</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Which of the following statement(s) is(are) true regarding the sound heard by the person ?",
    "image": null
  },
